					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393304#post-1264161</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393304/8-mr-moon#post-1264161</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 21 Sep 2011 22:49:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Anaxagoras</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1019930</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Now, obviously, there's no indication of any of this in the actual <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-917">Mr. Moon</a> article. I figure this isn't a problem, because, really, how's the Foundation going to figure out he can do this? I figured, as EndgamerAzari noted, that Mr. Moon seemed relatively bland compared to the others. This is my attempt to rectify that.</p> <p>Glad you all liked the tone. I wrote this the same day I wrote <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/1-mr-headless">Mr. Headless</a>, slightly earlier. My third story for this collection came significantly later. It's also significantly later in the post order. It'll be worth the wait.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
